This Python program calculates the sum of f(s)^k over all subsets of V using the prime factorization idea. It ensures that the answer is small enough (keeping modulo 10^9 + 7) by performing all calculations in powers of k modulo it. It iterates through each graph edge, adjusting the subsets' representation for possible edge additions to calculate the desired sum, adjusted by deleting any existing edges in the current path and multiplying by k for each resulting different combination of edges in consideration.

